        "title": "Prove the reflow no longer fires from a stray node click",
        "body": "Add or extend a test (tests/workspaceLoadFocus.test.js is the closest existing precedent) asserting: given two ready, non-manually-placed instances, clicking a node inside the non-anchor one does not change store.current.focusedGraphInstanceId and does not reposition the other instance. Then live-verify once against a running app (two graphs open in the workspace, click a node in the one that isn't focused, confirm the other one no longer jumps) — this bug was reported live and static analysis alone hasn't confirmed the fix yet.",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
