      "data": {
        "title": "Should selecting a node in a passive graph still pan the camera to center on it?",
        "body": "activate() and selectInstances() both call centerOnInstance() today. If selectNodeInInstance() keeps that call, the camera still visibly moves when you click a node in a passive graph — just without dragging any OTHER graph along with it. Is that still desired (bring the clicked graph into view) or should node-select leave the camera alone entirely and rely on the graph already being visible enough to click in the first place?",
